WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.518 --> 00:00:03.254
QUESTION HE WANTED TO ASK.

00:00:02.086 --> 00:00:03.621
CNN DENIES SCRIPTING

00:00:03.387 --> 00:00:04.355
ANYTHING.

00:00:03.754 --> 00:00:06.324
IN OTHER WORDS, THEY'RE

00:00:04.489 --> 00:00:07.725
CLAIMING THAT COLTON HAAB IS

00:00:06.457 --> 00:00:09.994
A LIAR.

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:10.561
COLTON HAAB JOINS US

00:00:10.128 --> 00:00:11.863
TONIGHT.

00:00:10.695 --> 00:00:12.330
COLTON, THANKS FOR COMING

00:00:11.996 --> 00:00:12.830
ON.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.498
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY.

00:00:12.964 --> 00:00:13.764
THANKS SO MUCH FOR HAVING

00:00:13.631 --> 00:00:14.665
ME.

00:00:13.898 --> 00:00:15.900
BEFORE WE GET INTO ANYTHING.

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:17.135
I JUST WANT TO MAKE SURE

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.935
THAT EVERYBODY HASN'T

00:00:17.268 --> 00:00:18.569
FORGOTTEN WHY WE ARE

00:00:18.069 --> 00:00:20.471
ACTUALLY HERE TONIGHT.

00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:21.839
I MEAN, WE LOST 17 LIVES

00:00:20.605 --> 00:00:22.373
LAST WEEK.

00:00:22.039 --> 00:00:23.441
&gt;&gt; Tucker: YES.

00:00:22.573 --> 00:00:24.275
&gt;&gt; I ACTUALLY PHYSICALLY PUT

00:00:23.574 --> 00:00:26.144
TWO TO REST TO.

00:00:24.408 --> 00:00:27.378
ME THAT WAS THE HARDEST

00:00:26.277 --> 00:00:28.312
THING TO ENDURE.

00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:28.646
NOBODY SHOULD HAVE TO GO

00:00:28.446 --> 00:00:29.313
THROUGH.

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:30.515
THIS AS LONG AS WE ARE

00:00:29.447 --> 00:00:31.482
TAKING THE RIGHT STEPS TO

00:00:30.648 --> 00:00:32.316
MOVE FORWARD FROM THIS AND

00:00:31.616 --> 00:00:33.851
MAKE SURE THIS DOESN'T

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.152
HAPPEN AGAIN, I'M ALL FOR

00:00:33.985 --> 00:00:35.686
THAT.

00:00:34.352 --> 00:00:36.053
&gt;&gt; WE CERTAINLY HAVEN'T

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.188
FORGOTTEN.

00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:37.688
THANK YOU FOR REMINDING US

00:00:37.321 --> 00:00:38.756
YET AGAIN.

00:00:37.822 --> 00:00:40.324
WE THINK THAT THE ONLY WAY

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.126
TO MAKE THE COUNTRY BETTER

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:44.562
AND MAYBE PUT A DENT IN THIS

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.796
SCOURGE IS TO HAVE A

00:00:44.695 --> 00:00:46.797
RATIONAL, THOUGHTFUL

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.832
CONVERSATION ABOUT WHAT TO

00:00:46.931 --> 00:00:50.568
DO NEXT.

00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:51.068
AND WITH THAT IN MIND.

00:00:50.768 --> 00:00:51.836
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY.

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:52.503
&gt;&gt; Tucker: YOU WERE PLANNING

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:54.772
TO GO TO THIS EVENT LAST

00:00:52.637 --> 00:00:56.007
NIGHT AND TELL ME IF I AM

00:00:54.906 --> 00:00:56.307
MISCHARACTERIZING ANY OF

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.375
THIS.

00:00:56.507 --> 00:00:58.309
&gt;&gt; NOW ARE NOT.

00:00:57.575 --> 00:00:59.377
&gt;&gt; Tucker: AT THE REQUEST OF

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:03.614
CNN PRODUCER YOU SENT IN A

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:05.416
NUMBER OF QUESTIONS

00:01:03.748 --> 00:01:06.484
QUESTIONS YOU WANTED TO ASK

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:09.387
ON THE STAGE AND THEY

00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:09.754
REWROTE ONE OF YOUR

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.221
QUESTIONS?

00:01:09.887 --> 00:01:10.688
IS THAT RIGHT?

00:01:10.355 --> 00:01:12.357
&gt;&gt; YES, SIR.

00:01:10.822 --> 00:01:13.758
WHAT HAD HAPPENED WAS FOUR

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.495
DAYS AGO I HAD GOTTEN

00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:19.897
CONTACT BY A LADY NAMED CNN.

00:01:17.628 --> 00:01:21.032
SHE HAD ASKED ME TO WRITE A

00:01:20.031 --> 00:01:21.466
SPEECH.

00:01:21.165 --> 00:01:22.467
TOWN HALL.

00:01:21.599 --> 00:01:23.434
SO I AGREED.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.303
I FELT LIKE IT WOULD BE THE

00:01:23.568 --> 00:01:27.872
RIGHT THING TO DO.

00:01:25.436 --> 00:01:28.973
BE ABLE TO GO SPEAK MY PART

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:30.007
AS WELL AS OPEN EYES TO A

00:01:29.107 --> 00:01:32.410
FEW THINGS THAT I THOUGHT

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:34.512
CAN MAKE THIS SITUATION A

00:01:32.543 --> 00:01:38.016
LITTLE BETTER.

00:01:34.645 --> 00:01:39.550
FOR THERE THREE DAYS AGO.

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:42.487
I GOUT AN EMAIL BACK FROM

00:01:39.684 --> 00:01:45.356
HER AND SHE ASKED FOR MORE

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.690
OF QUESTIONS RATHER THAN A

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:46.858
SPEECH.

00:01:45.823 --> 00:01:48.159
I SPEECH AND QUESTIONS I

00:01:46.991 --> 00:01:48.459
WANTED TO ASK AT THE TOWN

00:01:48.292 --> 00:01:49.660
HALL.

00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:50.895
THE DAY AFTER THAT IT WAS

00:01:49.794 --> 00:01:51.896
MORE OF JUST QUESTIONS.

00:01:51.029 --> 00:01:53.998
SHE ASKED FOR JUST QUESTIONS

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:55.633
THAT I WOULD LIKE TO ASK.

00:01:54.132 --> 00:01:57.635
SO, I GAVE HER MY QUESTIONS

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:58.937
AND THEN YESTERDAY, AT ABOUT

00:01:57.769 --> 00:01:59.204
5:15, I MADE CONTACT WITH

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.673
HER.

00:01:59.337 --> 00:02:03.241
AND SHE HAD ASKED IF I HAD

00:02:01.806 --> 00:02:04.309
JUST ASKED HER ONE QUESTION.

00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:05.377
SO WHAT THEY HAD ACTUALLY

00:02:04.442 --> 00:02:06.611
DONE WAS WROTE OUT A

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:08.413
QUESTION FOR ME BECAUSE IN

00:02:06.745 --> 00:02:09.814
MY INTERVIEW WITH CNN, I HAD

00:02:08.546 --> 00:02:10.582
TALKED ABOUT ARMING THE

00:02:09.948 --> 00:02:12.250
TEACHERS, IF THEY WERE

00:02:10.715 --> 00:02:14.119
WILLING TO ARM THEMSELVES IN

00:02:12.384 --> 00:02:14.453
THE SCHOOL TO CARRY ON

00:02:14.252 --> 00:02:16.455
CAMPUS.

00:02:14.586 --> 00:02:17.656
AND THEY HAD -- SHE HAD

00:02:16.588 --> 00:02:19.191
TAKEN THAT OF WHAT I HAD

00:02:17.789 --> 00:02:20.258
BRIEFED ON AND ACTUALLY

00:02:19.324 --> 00:02:20.525
WROTE THAT QUESTION OUT FOR

00:02:20.392 --> 00:02:21.660
ME.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:23.261
SO I HAVE THAT QUESTION HERE

00:02:21.793 --> 00:02:24.362
IF YOU WOULD LIKE ME TO ASK

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:25.130
IT FOR YOU.

00:02:24.563 --> 00:02:26.131
&gt;&gt; Tucker: I JUST WANT TO

00:02:25.263 --> 00:02:26.498
MAKE SURE I HAVE THIS

00:02:26.264 --> 00:02:28.600
STRAIGHT.

00:02:26.631 --> 00:02:31.069
SO YOU SENT THEM A LONG, IN

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:32.304
EFFECT, ESSAY ON WHAT YOU

00:02:31.203 --> 00:02:33.739
THOUGHT BUT THEY PUT THEIR

00:02:32.437 --> 00:02:34.906
OWN WORDS IN THE QUESTION

00:02:33.872 --> 00:02:36.408
AND THEY WEREN'T THE SAME AS

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.110
THE WORDS YOU HAD SENT IN?

00:02:36.541 --> 00:02:38.410
THEY WERE THE PRODUCER'S

00:02:38.243 --> 00:02:39.144
WORDS?

00:02:38.543 --> 00:02:40.512
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY.

00:02:39.277 --> 00:02:42.180
THEY HAD TAKEN WHAT I HAD

00:02:40.645 --> 00:02:43.315
WROTE AND WHAT I HAD BRIEFED

00:02:42.314 --> 00:02:45.784
ON AND TALKED ABOUT AND THEY

00:02:43.448 --> 00:02:51.390
ACTUALLY WROTE THE QUESTION

00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:52.257
FOR ME BUT NOT WITH THEIR

00:02:51.523 --> 00:02:54.059
WORDS EVEN AFTER THEY ASKED

00:02:52.391 --> 00:02:54.560
TO YOU SEND IN QUESTIONS.

00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:56.695
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.696
&gt;&gt; Tucker: THAT SEEMS

00:02:56.829 --> 00:02:58.397
DISHONEST.

00:02:57.896 --> 00:02:59.565
&gt;&gt; IT DEFINITELY DID.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.599
THAT'S KIND OF WHY I DIDN'T

00:02:59.698 --> 00:03:01.600
GO LAST NIGHT.

00:03:00.733 --> 00:03:03.369
ORIGINALLY I HAD THOUGHT

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:04.536
THAT IT WAS GOING TO BE MORE

00:03:03.502 --> 00:03:05.738
OF MY OWN QUESTION AND MY

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.139
OWN SAY AND THEN IT TURNED

00:03:05.871 --> 00:03:07.473
OUT TO BE MORE OF JUST A

00:03:07.273 --> 00:03:09.808
SCRIPT.

00:03:07.606 --> 00:03:11.176
AND SHE HAD ACTUALLY SAID

00:03:09.942 --> 00:03:12.077
THAT OVER THE PHONE THAT I

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.346
NEEDED TO STICK TO THE

00:03:12.211 --> 00:03:15.080
SCRIPT.

00:03:14.546 --> 00:03:17.483
&gt;&gt; THAT'S REMARKABLE.

00:03:15.214 --> 00:03:19.318
DID YOU WATCH LAST NIGHT?

00:03:17.616 --> 00:03:19.585
&gt;&gt; I WATCHED A LITTLE BIT OF

00:03:19.451 --> 00:03:22.655
IT.

00:03:19.718 --> 00:03:24.223
I KIND OF FELT LIKE I DIDN'T

00:03:22.788 --> 00:03:25.024
REALLY NEED TO BECAUSE I

00:03:24.356 --> 00:03:26.392
KNEW AS SOON AS WHAT HAD

00:03:25.157 --> 00:03:27.560
HAPPENED WITH ME THAT IT WAS

00:03:26.525 --> 00:03:30.729
GOING TO BE MORE SCRIPTED

00:03:27.693 --> 00:03:32.131
AND WASN'T ACTUALLY GOING TO

00:03:30.863 --> 00:03:32.832
BE ACTUAL QUESTIONS.

00:03:32.264 --> 00:03:35.234
THEN I DIDN'T FEEL THE NEED

00:03:32.965 --> 00:03:36.836
TO FULLY WATCH IT.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:38.671
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO IF CNN WAS

00:03:36.969 --> 00:03:39.605
WILLING TO REWORD YOUR

00:03:38.804 --> 00:03:40.539
QUESTION, PUT THEIR OWN

00:03:39.739 --> 00:03:41.741
WORDS IN YOUR MOUTH AND AS

00:03:40.673 --> 00:03:42.775
YOU SAID YOU DIDN'T WANT TO

00:03:41.874 --> 00:03:43.943
GO ALONG WITH THAT DO YOU

00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:47.947
THINK THEY DID THAT TO OTHER

00:03:44.076 --> 00:03:48.948
PEOPLE LAST NIGHT?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.750
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY, FROM WHAT DID

00:03:49.081 --> 00:03:52.184
I SEE, I SEEN A COUPLE

00:03:50.883 --> 00:03:53.352
PEOPLE THAT ASKED QUESTIONS

00:03:52.318 --> 00:03:54.420
BEFORE DID I LEAVE MY HOUSE.

00:03:53.486 --> 00:03:55.121
IT WAS A LITTLE PIECE OF

00:03:54.553 --> 00:03:56.555
PAPER CUT OUT.

00:03:55.254 --> 00:03:57.923
AND I KNOW FOR A FACT THAT

00:03:56.689 --> 00:03:59.358
NOBODY CUT THEIR OWN PAPER

00:03:58.057 --> 00:03:59.792
OUT AND WROTE THEIR OWN

00:03:59.492 --> 00:04:00.660
QUESTION.

00:03:59.925 --> 00:04:02.361
ESPECIALLY WHEN THEY WERE

00:04:00.793 --> 00:04:03.029
ALL BASED OFF THE SAME

00:04:02.495 --> 00:04:05.331
TOPIC.

00:04:03.162 --> 00:04:06.532
SO, TO ME, IT FROM RIGHT

00:04:05.464 --> 00:04:06.866
THERE IT SHOWED THIS ISN'T

00:04:06.666 --> 00:04:08.000
CORRECT.

00:04:06.999 --> 00:04:09.202
WHY DO THEY ALL HAVE THE

00:04:08.134 --> 00:04:10.269
SAME SIZE PIECE OF PAPER

00:04:09.335 --> 00:04:11.270
WITH A SHORT LITTLE QUESTION

00:04:10.403 --> 00:04:13.306
ON IT?

00:04:11.404 --> 00:04:15.441
SO, TO ME IT WAS A TOTAL

00:04:13.439 --> 00:04:16.309
WASTE OF MY TIME, HONESTLY.

00:04:15.642 --> 00:04:17.310
&gt;&gt; Tucker: YOU ARE NOT JUST

00:04:16.442 --> 00:04:18.711
SOME PERSON OFF THE STREET.

00:04:17.443 --> 00:04:19.078
YOU ARE A SURVIVOR OF THIS

00:04:18.845 --> 00:04:21.014
SHOOTING.

00:04:19.212 --> 00:04:23.182
AND THE POINT WAS TO LISTEN

00:04:21.147 --> 00:04:23.750
TO YOU, TO THE SURVIVORS OF

00:04:23.316 --> 00:04:24.984
THE SHOOTING.

00:04:23.883 --> 00:04:26.219
WERE YOU SURPRISED BY THE

00:04:25.118 --> 00:04:27.086
WAY THEY BEHAVED.

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:29.455
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.189
I MEAN, HONESTLY IT WAS VERY

00:04:29.589 --> 00:04:31.491
SHOCKING TO ME.

00:04:30.323 --> 00:04:33.693
BECAUSE WE JUST WENT THROUGH

00:04:31.624 --> 00:04:36.196
SUCH A HORRIFIC TRAGEDY FOR

00:04:33.826 --> 00:04:39.733
THEM TO TAKE THAT AND NOW

00:04:36.329 --> 00:04:42.769
MAKE SUCH A BIG NEWS OVER

00:04:39.866 --> 00:04:44.904
WHAT THEY WANT TO HEAR.

00:04:42.902 --> 00:04:45.772
VERY UPSETTING TO ME.

00:04:45.105 --> 00:04:47.640
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SHOCKING TO US

00:04:45.905 --> 00:04:48.007
TOO IN THE ACTUAL JOURNALISM

